{
  "summary": "Endorsed the round 6 over-engineering critique and proposed a concrete minimal v1 design: depends_on field with resolve_dependencies() and detect_cycle() in state.py, blocking only in auto-mode impl_stages with simple Kahn's algorithm topological sort, no plan_invalidation_check (use a dependency_warning flag instead of auto-moving features backward), no override tracking or dirty-flag caching (premature optimization), no dependency_events field (history entries suffice for v1), and dangling deps treated as blocking with a log warning. The design adds only ~150 lines of Python, ~20 lines of Go struct changes, and fits cleanly into the existing _cmd_move/_handle_edit patterns without new architectural concepts."
}
